 <br>
 
+#### 🫆 FINGERPRINT (OPTIONAL)
+
+Qylock asks PAM for the `qylock` service. To enable fingerprint unlock you need a matching PAM file with `pam_fprintd.so` in the auth stack.
+
+On **NixOS**, add this to your config:
+
+```nix
+services.fprintd.enable = true;
+security.pam.services.qylock = { };
+```
+
+`security.pam.services.<name>.fprintAuth` defaults to `config.services.fprintd.enable`, so fprintd is wired in automatically — same pattern as `security.pam.services.hyprlock`.
+
+On other distros, drop a file at `/etc/pam.d/qylock` modeled after your existing `hyprlock` / `login` PAM stack with `pam_fprintd.so` added.
+
+<br>
+
 
 
 <p align="center">━━━━━━━ ◈ ━━━━━━━</p>
